# Paths worth a second look before they reach main. NOT a gate: see the warning below.
#
#   .github/workflows/  is the Gate itself. A Run that weakened claude-review.yml or ci.yml
#                       would face no reviewer on the pull request after it.
#   db/migrations/      is the least reversible thing here. A bad schema change cannot be
#                       undone by reverting a commit.
#   docs/adr/0001       is the licensing rule this whole repo exists under.
#   CODEOWNERS          is this rule. It should not be editable by the thing it constrains.
#
# This file does not stop anything. The branch ruleset's only bypass actor is the admin role
# the Runs act as, and a Run's pull request is authored by Jack, who cannot approve his own.
# The review this file asks for is impossible rather than merely missing. See rolodeck-ai's
# docs/adr/0017, which worked this out the hard way.
#
# What the file is for is flagging: a pull request touching one of these paths should say so
# plainly in its body, because nothing else will.

/.github/workflows/              @fieldjw96
/db/migrations/                  @fieldjw96
/docs/adr/0001-only-openly-licensed-data.md  @fieldjw96
/.github/CODEOWNERS              @fieldjw96
